## LEG 2 (designed) — PIM-SM configured, and it STILL did not forward: finding F-13

  PIM-SM fully configured on both routers (adjacency up, RP mapping present on both, RPF route
  present on both).  Re-joined, re-measured:

    cap s2-pimsm-on-eth4.pcap: 6 frame(s)
      x5  ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f]
      x1  IP p103 10.38.22.66 -> 224.0.0.13 [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 01:00:5e:00:00:0d]

  0 of 5 for the joined group, and a PIM Hello from swi_a on the receiver segment.  Diagnosis,
  in the order it was done, because the mechanism is the finding:

    swi_a#show ip igmp groups
    Group Address    Interface            Uptime   Expires  Last Reporter
    239.1.1.1        vlan48               00:00:39 00:03:41 0.0.0.0        <- the group IS known
    swi_a#show ip pim sparse-mode local-members
    PIM Local membership information
    vlan48:                                                               <- and PIM knows NOTHING
    vlan61:
    swi_a#show ip pim sparse-mode mroute
    (*,G) Entries: 0        (S,G) Entries: 2        (S,G,rpt) Entries: 2
    (10.38.22.40, 239.1.1.1)   RPF nbr: 0.0.0.0  RPF idx: None  Upstream State: NOT JOINED

  Both preconditions were ruled out on the device, not assumed:
    swi_a#show ip pim sparse-mode rp mapping -> Group(s): 224.0.0.0/4, Static  RP: 10.0.61.2
                                                Uptime: 00:04:38   (so it predates the failure)
    swi_a#show ip route 10.38.22.40          -> Routing entry for 10.38.22.32/27
                                                Known via "static", * via 10.0.61.1, vlan61
  And the report itself was confirmed correct ON THE WIRE, not inferred from the tool:
    sniff of eth4, 16 s:  x2  IP p2 10.38.22.70 -> 239.1.1.1
                              [eth 00:11:22:33:44:77 -> 01:00:5e:01:01:01]
  i.e. a well-formed IGMPv2 report from a real on-subnet source.  Then:

    swi_a#show ip igmp interface vlan48
    Interface vlan48 (Index 348)
     IGMP Disabled, Active(Snoop Only), Non-Querier, Version 3 (default)     <- THE CAUSE
     IGMP interface has 1 group-record states
     IGMP activity: 2 joins, 0 leaves
     IGMP querying router is 0.0.0.0

  **`ip pim sparse-mode` on an interface does NOT enable the router-side IGMP on it.**  The
  membership shown by `show ip igmp groups` was learned by **IGMP SNOOPING**, which is enabled by
  default, and snooping does not feed PIM.  One command fixed it:

    swi_a(config-if)#ip igmp
    swi_a#show ip igmp interface vlan48
     IGMP Enabled, Active, Querier, Version 3 (default)
    swi_a#show ip pim sparse-mode local-members
    vlan48:
      (*, 239.1.1.1) : Include                                              <- PIM sees it now

  => **F-13** (new): on this build a receiver interface needs BOTH `ip pim sparse-mode` and an
  explicit `ip igmp`.  Until `ip igmp` is given, `show ip igmp groups` lists the group with a
  live expiry timer while `show ip pim sparse-mode local-members` is empty and the dataplane
  forwards nothing — two read-backs disagreeing at the same instant, with the dataplane
  following the second.  Same family as the x960 mirroring trap (x960.md 5) where `show mirror`
  read Enabled while nothing was copied.  Detail and severity in the queue's `## Issues`.
  VERDICT leg 2: the leg is a PASS as a measurement (it correctly reported no forwarding) and
  it produced F-13.

