      x5  ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f]

  => the LEFT group 239.3.3.3 **0 of 5**; the still-joined group 239.2.2.2 **5 of 5**, in the
     same leg, same instant, same wire.  The prune is real and it is group-specific.
  VERDICT leg 5: PASS.

## LEG 6 (designed) — the RP's role isolated by A/B on one group

  The queue asks specifically that "the RP's role is the thing to isolate".  Done on a single
  group with nothing else changed between the two halves.

  (a) `no ip pim rp-address 10.0.61.2` on BOTH routers (`show ip pim sparse-mode rp mapping` on
      swi_a then prints the header and no mapping), THEN join 239.4.4.4 and measure:

    cap s9-no-rp-eth4.pcap: 12 frame(s)
      x10 ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f]
      x1  IP p103 10.38.22.66 -> 224.0.0.13  (swi_a PIM Hello)
      x1  IP p2   10.38.22.66 -> 224.0.0.1   (swi_a IGMP general query — it IS the querier now)

    => **0 of 10** for a group that is JOINED, while the instrument control is 10 of 10.

  (b) `ip pim rp-address 10.0.61.2` restored on both, same group, membership untouched:

    cap s10-rp-restored-eth4.pcap: 19 frame(s)
      x10 ICMP t8/c0 ... 10/10
      x8  UDP 10.38.22.40 -> 239.4.4.4 :5001 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 01:00:5e:04:04:04]

    => **8 of 10** (the usual 2 frames consumed building the tree, cf. leg 4).
  => The RP is load-bearing, and the ONLY variable between 0/10 and 8/10 was the RP mapping.
  VERDICT leg 6: PASS.

## LEG 7 (designed, satisfactory-level) — persistence across a reboot

  Reboot-persistence without touching startup-config, by the queue's technique:

    awplus#copy running-config flash:/ck43863.cfg        -> Successful operation
    awplus(config)#boot config-file flash:/ck43863.cfg
    awplus#show boot -> Current boot config: flash:/ck43863.cfg (file exists)
    tools/tb ckreload tb277 ckt1406c u2 115200 480
      reboot question: 'reboot system? (y/n):' -> y ;  login seen after 61 s

  swi_a was NOT reloaded (RISK-1) and stayed up throughout.  After the reload, BEFORE measuring:

    awplus#show boot -> Current boot config: flash:/ck43863.cfg (file exists)
    awplus#show ip pim sparse-mode neighbor -> 10.0.61.2 vlan61 00:00:14/00:01:31 v2 1 / DR
    awplus#show ip interface brief -> vlan10 10.38.22.34/27, vlan48 unassigned, vlan61 10.0.61.1/30
    awplus#show spanning-tree brief   (first read, ~30 s after login)
      port1.0.4 Designated Forwarding   port1.0.10 Designated Forwarding
      port1.0.48 Designated **Discarding**        <- the known 17-21 s post-reload window
    awplus#show spanning-tree brief   (re-read)
      port1.0.4 / port1.0.10 / port1.0.48 all Designated Forwarding   <- only now is it safe

  Then a group never used before the reload (239.5.5.5) was joined and measured:

    cap s11-postreload-eth4.pcap: 20 frame(s)
      x10 ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours]  (10/10 instrument control)
      x8  UDP 10.38.22.40 -> 239.5.5.5 :5001 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 01:00:5e:05:05:05]
      x1  IP p103 10.38.22.66 -> 224.0.0.13   x1  IP p2 10.38.22.66 -> 224.0.0.1

  => 8 of 10 for the new group, **0 of 10** for the never-joined control 239.9.9.9 in the same
     leg, 10/10 instrument control.  The configuration survived the reboot AND the DATAPLANE
     works after it, which is the half a `show running-config` cannot prove.
  Boot pointer put back and the staged file removed:
    awplus(config)#boot config-file flash:/default.cfg
    awplus#delete flash:/ck43863.cfg -> Delete flash:/ck43863.cfg? (y/n)[n]:y -> Successful operation
    awplus#show boot -> Current boot config: flash:/default.cfg (file exists)
    awplus#dir flash:/*.cfg -> 1049 -rw- Oct 15 2026 10:49:02  flash:/default.cfg   (only that)
  VERDICT leg 7: PASS.

