## Steps skipped

  None.  Two PIM-SM limbs this topology cannot reach are named rather than silently omitted:
  **Assert** (it needs two PIM routers on ONE shared segment, and this bench's only multi-router
  segment is a /30) and **BSR/candidate-RP** election (`ip pim bsr-candidate` /
  `ip pim rp-candidate` exist on the DUT but a dynamic RP election needs a third PIM router;
  only two units on this bench hold the PIM licence).  Static RP was used, which the queue names
  as the simplest and which exercised the Register path fully.

VERDICT: PASS -- designed from the protocol and the CLI surface (no authored step text exists); baseline off proven with a joined receiver, PIM-SM forwarding proven 5/5 with a never-joined control group at 0/5 and an instrument control in every leg, the Register / RP-Join / Register-Stop / SPT sequence decoded on the transit wire, prune-on-leave proven group-specific, the RP isolated by A/B on one group (0/10 -> 8/10), and removal and reboot persistence both proven in the dataplane. Produced F-13, O-20..O-23 and two generic tool fixes.
